# NextLaunch Pro Cursor IDE Rules

You are working on NextLaunch Pro, an enterprise-grade full-stack SaaS boilerplate built with:
- Next.js 16 (App Router with Turbopack)
- React 19 (Server Actions, Optimistic updates)
- TypeScript (Strict mode, zero `any` types)
- Tailwind CSS (PreFlight Flat White & Blue Design System)
- Polar Merchant of Record SDK & Subscriptions
- Prisma ORM with PostgreSQL / SQLite

## Guidelines
1. Always keep server logic and client logic cleanly separated. Use `'use client'` only when state, event handlers, or browser APIs are needed.
2. Use `@/lib/db` for database queries and `@/lib/polar` for billing logic.
3. Adhere to the DevPreFlight flat UI design tokens: avoid generic colors, use crisp high-contrast white & blue tokens (`bg-white`, `border-slate-200`, `text-slate-900`, `bg-blue-600`).
4. Keep all components accessible (WCAG AAA compliant).
